## Flight Planning & Booking {#flight-planning-booking}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.google.com/travel/flights" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Google Flights</h4>
    <p>The best all-around flight search. Date grid and price graph make it easy to find the cheapest days to fly. Price tracking sends alerts when fares drop. Covers most airlines worldwide.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.skyscanner.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Skyscanner</h4>
    <p>Great for "everywhere" searches if you're flexible on destination. Also searches hotels and car rentals. Useful for finding the cheapest destination from your airport.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://skiplagged.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Skiplagged</h4>
    <p>Finds "hidden city" ticketing deals where booking a flight with a layover at your actual destination is cheaper than a direct flight. Read their FAQ about baggage rules before trying this.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Train & Ground Transport {#train-ground-transport}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.seat61.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Seat 61</h4>
    <p>The definitive guide to train travel worldwide. Every route, every station, every booking link. If you want to travel by train anywhere on earth, start here. Includes ferry connections too.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://stationview.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Station View</h4>
    <p>Live train departure boards for the UK, France, Switzerland, Belgium, Germany, Netherlands, Finland, and Japan. Clean interface that shows exactly what the station screens show.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Maps & Navigation {#maps-navigation}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://maps.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Google Maps</h4>
    <p>The most comprehensive map service. Real-time traffic, public transit directions, street view, business hours and reviews, offline maps for specific areas. Hard to beat for daily use.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://maps.apple.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Apple Maps</h4>
    <p>Privacy-focused alternative to Google Maps. Excellent turn-by-turn navigation, detailed city maps with elevation, and offline support. Improving rapidly with each iOS update.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.waze.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Waze</h4>
    <p>Crowdsourced navigation that excels at real-time traffic, police alerts, and road hazard warnings. Best for daily driving in urban areas where traffic changes quickly.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.bing.com/maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Bing Maps</h4>
    <p>Solid alternative with bird's eye aerial imagery and Ordnance Survey maps for the UK. Useful when Google Maps is blocked or you need a different perspective.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://f-droid.org/packages/net.osmand.plus/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>OsmAnd</h4>
    <p>OpenStreetMap-based offline navigation with full turn-by-turn directions. No internet connection needed once maps are downloaded. Includes hiking trails, POIs, and topographic data. Available on F-Droid.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://comaps.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>CoMaps</h4>
    <p>Privacy-first offline maps app (a fork of Organic Maps). No ads, no tracking, no account required. Uses OpenStreetMap data. Lightweight and fast.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://bikesharingworldmap.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Bike-Sharing World Map</h4>
    <p>Interactive map showing every bike-sharing system worldwide with station locations, bike availability, and docking info. Essential for exploring cities on two wheels.</p>
  </a>
</div>

<div class="about-tip reveal">
  <span class="tip-icon">💡</span>
  <span><strong>Tip:</strong> Before traveling abroad, download offline maps for your destination in both Google Maps and OsmAnd/OAM. Cell service isn't always reliable, and having a backup map app can save you when one doesn't have the area well-covered.</span>
</div>

## Accommodation {#accommodation}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://cozycozy.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>CozyCozy</h4>
    <p>Metasearch for accommodation that compares Booking.com, Airbnb, Vrbo, Hotels.com, and more in one place. Saves time checking multiple sites for the best price.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://trustroots.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Trustroots</h4>
    <p>Hospitality exchange network focused on travelers, hitchhikers, and nomads. Free to use, community-driven. Think Couchsurfing but without the commercialization.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Passport, Visa & Entry Requirements {#passport-visa-entry-requirements}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.entryconditions.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Entry Conditions</h4>
    <p>Shows entry requirements, visa policies, and passport validity rules for every country. Also check <a href="https://www.entryconditions.com/passport/united-states" target="_blank">US-specific passport info</a>.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://visaindex.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Visa Index</h4>
    <p>Check visa requirements by passport. Shows which countries you can visit visa-free, visa-on-arrival, or need to apply in advance. Updated regularly.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Weather & Environment {#weather-environment}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.windy.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Windy</h4>
    <p>Beautiful, interactive weather map with wind, rain, temperature, waves, and air quality layers. Uses multiple forecast models (ECMWF, GFS, NAM). Indispensable for outdoor travel planning.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.ventusky.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Ventusky</h4>
    <p>Another excellent weather visualization platform. Shows precipitation, wind, pressure, and more with a clean interface. Good complement to Windy for cross-checking forecasts.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://floodmap.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Flood Map</h4>
    <p>Elevation and flood risk maps for any location. Useful for checking whether your destination might be affected by seasonal flooding, storm surges, or rising sea levels.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://sitinshade.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Sit in Shade</h4>
    <p>Find shaded spots along transit routes or at specific locations based on sun position. Perfect for planning walks in hot climates or finding a cool spot to rest.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Destination Inspiration {#destination-inspiration}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.atlasobscura.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Atlas Obscura</h4>
    <p>The definitive guide to the world's weirdest, most wonderful places. Abandoned buildings, natural oddities, unusual museums, hidden tunnels — if it's strange and worth seeing, it's here.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>UNESCO World Heritage List</h4>
    <p>Every UNESCO World Heritage site, searchable by country and year. The gold standard for culturally and naturally significant destinations worth planning a trip around.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.roadsideamerica.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Roadside America</h4>
    <p>The ultimate guide to quirky roadside attractions across the United States. Giant statues, bizarre museums, unusual architecture — perfect for road trip planning.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://en.wikivoyage.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Wikivoyage</h4>
    <p>Free, up-to-date travel wiki maintained by volunteers. More active than Wikitravel. Covers destinations worldwide with practical info on transportation, safety, and sights.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://wikitravel.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Wikitravel</h4>
    <p>Older travel wiki with extensive destination guides. Some content overlaps with Wikivoyage but worth checking both for older, more detailed articles on certain regions.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Cultural & Etiquette Guides {#cultural-etiquette-guides}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://culturalatlas.sbs.com.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Cultural Atlas</h4>
    <p>Country-by-country guide to cultural norms, etiquette, communication styles, and business practices. Invaluable for avoiding social faux pas when traveling somewhere unfamiliar.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Special Interest Travel {#special-interest-travel}

<div class="card-grid-2">
  <a href="https://www.rcdb.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>RCDB (Roller Coaster Database)</h4>
    <p>The most comprehensive database of roller coasters worldwide. Every coaster, every park, every stat. Plan a theme park trip around the best coasters in any region.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.darkridedatabase.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Dark Ride Database</h4>
    <p>Catalog of dark rides (indoor tracked attractions) at amusement parks worldwide. Covers classic dark rides, interactive shooters, and modern trackless systems.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://flightradar24.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Flightradar24</h4>
    <p>Live flight tracking showing real-time aircraft positions, routes, altitudes, and speeds. Fun for spotting planes overhead and useful for checking flight status from the ground.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.flightaware.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>FlightAware</h4>
    <p>More detailed than FR24 for flight tracking and status. Better for actual flight planning — shows delays, cancellations, aircraft history, and airport conditions in more depth.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://planefinder.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Plane Finder</h4>
    <p>Alternative flight tracker with a clean interface. Shows aircraft photos, flight paths, and estimated arrival times. Good when FR24 or FA are overloaded.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://globe.adsbexchange.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>ADS-B Exchange</h4>
    <p>Community-driven flight tracking that doesn't filter military or private aircraft. The most complete picture of what's actually in the sky. No block lists.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://airplanes.live/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Airplanes.Live</h4>
    <p>ADS-B flight tracking with a modern 3D view. Open-source platform. Also has companion <a href="https://github.com/d4rken-org/airplanes-live-app" target="_blank">Android app</a> for on-the-go tracking.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="https://objectiveunclear.com/airloom.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="shared-card reveal">
    <h4>Air Loom</h4>
    <p>3D visualization of live flight paths. Watch aircraft move through space in a three-dimensional view. More of an art piece than a utility, but mesmerizing to explore.</p>
  </a>
</div>

## Essential Tools {#essential-tools}

<div class="resource-grid">
  <a href="https://www.esimdb.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=esimdb.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="eSIMDB favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>eSIMDB</h4>
      <p>Compare eSIM data plans from every provider worldwide. Find the cheapest data for your destination without hunting through individual carrier sites.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.airnavradar.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=airnavradar.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="AirNav Radar favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>AirNav Radar</h4>
      <p>Another live flight tracker with a focus on detailed aircraft and airport information. Good for aviation enthusiasts who want more than just position data.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://flight-viz.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=flight-viz.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="Flight-Viz favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>Flight-Viz</h4>
      <p>Beautiful visualization powered by ADS-B data. See global air traffic patterns in real time.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.tropicaltidbits.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=tropicaltidbits.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="Tropical Tidbits favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>Tropical Tidbits</h4>
      <p>Advanced weather models and tropical cyclone tracking. Best for meteorology enthusiasts and travelers heading to hurricane-prone regions.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://www.xweather.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=xweather.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="XWeather favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>XWeather</h4>
      <p>Live weather maps with radar, satellite, and severe weather alerts. Clean interface good for quick checks.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://143190.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=143190.xyz&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="143190 favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>143190.xyz — IMAX Theatres</h4>
      <p>IMAX theatre database showing locations, screen types (GT, SR, Xenon, Laser), and audio systems worldwide. For cinephiles who plan trips around the best screens.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a href="https://frightfind.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="resource-card reveal">
    <img loading="lazy" src="https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=frightfind.com&sz=32" width="24" height="24" class="resource-favicon" alt="FrightFind favicon" />
    <div class="resource-body">
      <h4>FrightFind</h4>
      <p>Find haunted houses, haunted attractions, and Halloween events near you or at your destination. Seasonal but useful for October travel planning.</p>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>

<div class="about-tip reveal">
  <span class="tip-icon">💡</span>
  <span><strong>Tip:</strong> Get an eSIM before you travel. eSIMDB lets you compare plans so you can grab a local data plan without hunting for a physical SIM. Most modern phones support eSIM — check your model before assuming you need a physical card.</span>
</div>

## Further Reading {#further-reading}

- [Seat 61](https://www.seat61.com/) — Everything you need to know about train travel worldwide
- [Wikivoyage](https://en.wikivoyage.org/) — Free, open-source travel guides for every destination
- [Atlas Obscura](https://www.atlasobscura.com/) — The world's most unusual places
- [UNESCO World Heritage List](https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/) — Culturally and naturally significant sites
- [Cultural Atlas](https://culturalatlas.sbs.com.au/) — Country-by-country etiquette and cultural norms
- [Roadside America](https://www.roadsideamerica.com/) — Quirky roadside attractions across the US
- [Windy](https://www.windy.com/) — Interactive weather maps for trip planning
- [Bike-Sharing World Map](https://bikesharingworldmap.com/) — Find bike-share stations everywhere
- [Flood Map](https://floodmap.net/) — Elevation and flood risk data for any location
- [Sit in Shade](https://sitinshade.com/) — Find shade based on sun position
- [Entry Conditions](https://www.entryconditions.com/) — Visa and passport requirements
- [Visa Index](https://visaindex.com/) — Visa-free travel by passport

